# Hosts that cannot be checked from CI, and why.
#
# Every entry here is a host that refuses unauthenticated or datacenter
# traffic, not a link that is broken. lychee's --accept is global rather than
# per-domain, so accepting these status codes would accept them everywhere and
# mask a genuine break on some other host. Skipping the domain is the only
# per-domain lever lychee offers. See .github/workflows/links.yml for the
# matching --accept note.
#
# Before adding a host here, confirm it is actually unreachable from a GitHub
# runner rather than merely slow - compare a local `curl -w %{time_total}`
# against the CI log. Slow is a --timeout problem; blocked is this file.

# Unsplash and Pexels blanket-reject unauthenticated/bot traffic on these
# photo/photographer-credit links (401/403 depending on the request).
unsplash\.com
pexels\.com

# Instagram answers unauthenticated datacenter traffic with 429 and then
# redirect-loops to /accounts/login (10+ hops observed in run 34786169023).
# 429 is deliberately not accepted globally - see #74 - because it means the
# link was never checked, so the domain is skipped instead.
instagram\.com

# bb.ringingworld.co.uk responds in ~0.54s from a UK connection but never
# answers a GitHub runner at all: [TIMEOUT] on every attempt in run
# 34786169023, at a 15s timeout. That is a cloud/geo block, not slowness, so
# no timeout value would fix it. The links are correct; check them locally.
bb\.ringingworld\.co\.uk
